: fixture: anthropic-messages/04-midstream-error.sse
: protocol: Anthropic Messages API, streaming; HTTP status was 200, then an error event arrives mid-stream
: provenance: CONSTRUCTED by R2. The final "error" event payload is COPIED VERBATIM from
:   https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/streaming ("Error events", checked 2026-11-11).
:   The preceding events are constructed from the documented schema.
: doc facts: overloaded_error "would normally correspond to an HTTP 529 in a non-streaming context";
:   errors can occur after the API returns 200 (https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/errors, checked 2026-11-11).
: note: there is no message_delta / message_stop after the error; the server ends the stream.
: note: the tool_use block at index 1 never reaches content_block_stop. It MUST NOT produce ToolCallReady.
: expected ModelEvents: TextDelta("I'll look that up"), ToolCallDelta(...) (optional, UI only),
:   Failed(kind=overloaded, retryable=true, partial_output_emitted=true, provider_type="overloaded_error").
:   No Usage event is guaranteed: usage is unknown, not zero.

event: message_start
data: {"type":"message_start","message":{"id":"msg_01MIDSTREAMERRORFIXTURE01","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","content":[],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":120,"output_tokens":1}}}

event: content_block_start
data: {"type":"content_block_start","index":0,"content_block":{"type":"text","text":""}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"I'll look that up"}}

event: content_block_stop
data: {"type":"content_block_stop","index":0}

event: content_block_start
data: {"type":"content_block_start","index":1,"content_block":{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CUTOFFCUTOFFCUTOFFCUTOF","name":"read_file","input":{}}}

event: content_block_delta
